  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1246 AM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nThe second half of the workweek looks great with the drier air in \nthe wake of the front. This keeps the afternoons mild but with a \ngreater comfortability with lower humidity. The mornings are to \ntrend cooler under mostly clear skies.\n\nChanges then arrive through the weekend with a progressive moving \nshortwave arriving out of Mexico from the west. While the medium \nguidance is in fair agreement, some additional changes could be \npossible in the long run, especially with the potential of any \nphasing with additional upper level energy located across the \nIntermountain West. Overall, rain chances (30-60%) look to make a \nreturn across the region, peaking from late Saturday into early \nSunday. A cold front may then work into the mix sometime towards \nMonday or Monday night pending the evolution of that second upper \nlevel system coming out of the Intermountain West and into the \nCentral Plains.",
